// BT-3625 (ADR 0127 §3/§10): a Value class's `uses:` provision must reach
// compiled Core Erlang output through the existing value-type generator
// unchanged — and, because the protocol lives in its own file
// (`describable.bt`, as ADR 0127 requires), the flattened method's BEAM line
// annotation must carry the *protocol's* file and line, not `main.bt`'s.
//
// `describable.bt` is the cross-file protocol carrier: the harness hands its
// parsed protocol to `analyse_full` as `pre_loaded_protocol_defs`, the way the
// CLI build's Pass 1 does.

Value subclass: Report
  uses: Describable

  title -> String => "Report"
